// Brought to u by MidManStudio
//
// Ships: the burger-menu Settings sheet (one toggle: show/hide the
// debug panel), and the note editor's real bold/italic/underline/
// strikethrough/font-size — previously the toolbar just inserted literal
// **/__ characters because the editor was a plain <textarea>, which
// cannot render mixed formatting at all regardless of what the toolbar
// logic did. NoteContent is now a real contenteditable div; formatting
// runs through the browser's native Selection/execCommand API, which is
// what makes "applies to the selection if one exists, otherwise sets
// sticky style for whatever's typed next" work without hand-rolling
// either half of it — see src/lib/utils/richText.ts's own header
// comment for the full rationale and the honest caveats (execCommand is
// deprecated-but-still-implemented in Chromium/Android WebView; none of
// this can be exercised by scripts/smoke-test.mjs since jsdom doesn't
// implement execCommand at all — confirmed empirically, not assumed).
// note.content is HTML now instead of markdown-ish plain text (still
// just a `string` field — no schema change). Ripple-effect fixes
// included so nothing silently regressed: NoteCard's preview and the
// landing page's search now strip HTML tags, the AI note creator
// escapes its plain-text output into safe HTML, and the .txt export
// converts back to plain text instead of dumping raw markup.
//
// Every other file next to this manifest is real, verbatim content,
// delivered as one .tar.gz. This time every entry sits NESTED inside
// the archive at its real path under src/ (not flat + overrides, unlike
// the previous effect-fix bundle) — none of these paths have a
// dot-prefixed directory component, so the stage_replacements_dir()/
// collect_candidates() dot-directory pruning issue that forced the flat
// + overrides:: workaround for .github/workflows/ci-baby.yml last time
// simply doesn't apply here. Nested resolution pins each file to its
// real destination directly, no overrides:: needed.
//
// NOT included in this bundle, and not something the replacements
// system does at all (it's additive/overwrite-only — no delete
// mechanism in the flow this manifest uses): src/lib/utils/textEditing.ts
// and src/lib/utils/roman.ts are now dead code (their entire reason
// to exist — plain-text markdown-marker wrapping and regex-based list
// handling — is replaced by native contenteditable + execCommand) and
// need a manual `git rm src/lib/utils/textEditing.ts src/lib/utils/roman.ts`
// after this lands. Confirmed via grep against the whole src/ tree that
// nothing else imports from either file before recommending the delete.

@CONFIG(
  version    -> "1.0.0"
  author     -> "Mid-D-Man"
  features   -> "data"
  debug_mode -> "off"
)

@DATA(
  target_root = "."
)
